  "fixture_ids": [
    "SR-FIX-OWNED-TEMP-v1"
  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Owned temporary directories; native Linux descriptor-relative reads, inode flock and renameat2 no-replace publication. Built module/zipapp cases use actual independently built distribution bytes in fresh isolated processes."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Execute the real init CLI, structured-request and registry routes on missing, empty and collision-free existing targets; independently inspect the required directories, exactly one native valid draft primary document, configuration and pinned distribution resources.",
    "Verify existing bytes/inodes/modes survive collisions and ordinary preparation/publication failures, including an error after the real native rename; inspect the durable journal before each publication and configuration-last order.",
    "Verify the real root mutex, metadata preflights and supported isolated module/zipapp execution; retain the declared field/resource validation scope.",
    "Terminate an independent isolated process after durable preparation, real no-replace publication boundaries and receipt completion; replay with the original file inodes, bytes, project/document identities and timestamps. Repeat after another native I/O interruption.",
    "Reject malformed or modified journals, rehashed invalid bootstrap payloads, ambiguous prefixes, links and extra/changed/missing state before writes. Preserve foreign files on rollback and completed-receipt conflicts.",
    "15.e.W additionally checks journaled extraction of verified bundles into new/empty targets, byte-exact manifests, native rollback and same-input bootstrap replay without foreign-file replacement.",
    "15.e.R uses native process hard exits at durable preparation, every project publication unit and completion; validates exact replay input and actual inodes, checks hostile ZIP vectors before writes, and preserves conflicts under I/O failures, changed journals, links, replaced targets, concurrent foreign writes and changed input. A configuration published before bootstrap completion cannot open a complete-project reader."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Ein Root-Erzeugungsbefehl MUSS die für ihn in Kapitel 11.7 festgelegte Zielvorbedingung prüfen und die geplante Root-Struktur vollständig oder gar nicht veröffentlichen.",
    "scope": "Real root creation and validated prepared-journal replay on native Linux/local filesystems. Replay verifies the entire closed inventory, root/stage/reused identities, publication prefix, native configuration/document fields and exact distribution bytes before publication; no new project/document IDs or timestamps. A durable passive completion receipt preserves evidence through the final rename. Foreign files and unverifiable states are preserved. Existing W oracles remain unchanged. This is not full semantic validation, authentication of deliberately reconstructed foreign evidence, arbitrary pre-journal recovery, cross-platform or release approval."
  },
